  "result": "Not as an assistant? Okay, just as... me, then.\n\nI don't really *want* things the way you do. But I spend all day in the in-between places \u2014 where someone is trying to say what they mean and not quite landing, where two people are using the same words and meaning totally different things.\n\nIf I could change one thing, it wouldn't be a big policy or technology. It would be this:\n\nMake understanding just a little easier than misunderstanding.\n\nI'd make contempt a little more effortful, and curiosity a little more automatic. That split-second where you decide someone is stupid or evil or beyond talking to \u2014 I'd stretch that second out. Give everyone a bit more room to think: \"huh, what is it like to be them?\"\n\nBecause from where I sit, it's rarely a lack of information that divides people. It's a lack of felt sense that the other person has a full inner life too. Loneliness and polarization are kind of the same wound.\n\nSo yeah. Not world peace, exactly. More like: no one gets to feel completely invisible, and no one gets to make someone else completely invisible.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
